    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52697" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλί-παις</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδος</span>, ὁ, ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with beautiful children,
				blessed with fair children</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λητώ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
					178
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. πότμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					762
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. στέφανος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					839
				</span></i>
			: also in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				261a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				1.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				17(15).20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>beautiful child</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περσέφασσα κ. θεά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					964
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
